    "logic_explanation": "<ul style='margin-top: 5px; padding-left: 20px;'><li style='margin-bottom: 6px;'><strong>The Variant:</strong> NLRP3 c.2798G>T → a missense at exon 8 (p.G933V). SpliceAI predicts exon-internal <b>donor gain</b> (DS 0.28, Δ-2 bp); splice product below.</li><li style='margin-bottom: 6px;'><strong>Exon-numbering note:</strong> Also referenced under legacy nomenclature as <b>VEP/SnpEff coding-only exon 7/9 (5′-UTR exons excluded from count)</b>. The exon number above follows the modern MANE/RefSeq transcript model (which counts every exon, including 5′-UTR-only exons); legacy clinical literature may number exons differently.</li><li style='margin-bottom: 6px;'><a href='https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/Q96P20/entry#family_and_domains' target='_blank' style='text-decoration: underline; color: #4338ca;'>UniProt</a>: No domain of interest.</li><li style='margin-bottom: 6px;'><strong>Allelic & locus context:</strong> Alternate isoform HGVS (same ClinVar VID 3583456): 10 other transcript/genomic name(s) from your ClinVar record were included in literature search (not your curated NM numbering).</li><li style='margin-bottom: 6px;'><strong>Splice products:</strong> <b>Product 1 (primary) — exon-internal donor gain:</b><br><b>SpliceAI signal:</b> <b>exon-internal donor gain</b> — DS_DG 0.28 at Δ−2 bp from variant.<br><b>Geometry:</b> cryptic site at cDNA position <code>2796</code> inside coding exon 8 — new 5&prime; splice donor truncates the 3&prime; end of the exon (<b>38 nt</b> removed from the mature mRNA ORF) net ORF change: 38 nt deleted.<br><b>Frame:</b> <b>out-of-frame</b>.<br><b>Junction codon:</b> reading frame shifts at codon 933 (p.Gly933 → p.Ile933… in mutant ORF).<br><b>Predicted protein:</b> <code>p.Ile933fsTer33</code> (33 aa before stop in shifted frame).<br><b>Premature termination:</b> PTC in exon 9/10 at native c.2931-c.2933 (<code>TGA</code>) — frame-shifted stop codon.<br><b>Protein length:</b> truncated ≈ 964/1034 aa (6.8% C-terminus lost if this product is translated).<br><b>NMD:</b> predicted (PTC in penultimate exon 9/10, 72 nt from last exon-exon junction; ≥50 nt rule).<br><span style='color:#94a3b8;font-size:0.88em'>Exon-internal model — GT/AG dinucleotides at splice sites are excluded from ORF body counts on deep-intronic maps.</span></li></ul>",
    "logic_explanation_plaintext": "The Variant: NLRP3 c.2798G>T → a missense at exon 8 (p.G933V). SpliceAI predicts exon-internal donor gain (DS 0.28, Δ-2 bp); splice product below.\n\nExon-numbering note: Also referenced under legacy nomenclature as VEP/SnpEff coding-only exon 7/9 (5′-UTR exons excluded from count). The exon number above follows the modern MANE/RefSeq transcript model (which counts every exon, including 5′-UTR-only exons); legacy clinical literature may number exons differently.\n\nUniProt: No domain of interest.\n\nAllelic & locus context: Alternate isoform HGVS (same ClinVar VID 3583456): 10 other transcript/genomic name(s) from your ClinVar record were included in literature search (not your curated NM numbering).\n\nSplice products:\nProduct 1 (primary) — exon-internal donor gain:\nSpliceAI signal: exon-internal donor gain — DS_DG 0.28 at Δ−2 bp from variant.\nGeometry: cryptic site at cDNA position 2796 inside coding exon 8 — new 5′ splice donor truncates the 3′ end of the exon (38 nt removed from the mature mRNA ORF) net ORF change: 38 nt deleted.\nFrame: out-of-frame.\nJunction codon: reading frame shifts at codon 933 (p.Gly933 → p.Ile933… in mutant ORF).\nPredicted protein: p.Ile933fsTer33 (33 aa before stop in shifted frame).\nPremature termination: PTC in exon 9/10 at native c.2931-c.2933 (TGA) — frame-shifted stop codon.\nProtein length: truncated ≈ 964/1034 aa (6.8% C-terminus lost if this product is translated).\nNMD: predicted (PTC in penultimate exon 9/10, 72 nt from last exon-exon junction; ≥50 nt rule).\nExon-internal model — GT/AG dinucleotides at splice sites are excluded from ORF body counts on deep-intronic maps.",
